      "@id": "kt:data-parallelism",
      "@type": "kto:Technique",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Data parallelism",
      "skos:definition": "A way to scale neural-network training in which every device holds a full replica of the model, processes a different slice of each minibatch, and averages gradients with its peers (typically via all-reduce) so that all replicas take the same optimizer step.",
