    {
      "@id": "kt:gptq",
      "@type": "kto:Algorithm",
      "skos:prefLabel": "GPTQ",
      "skos:definition": "A one-shot post-training weight-quantization algorithm for large transformer language models that rounds each layer's weights to 3 or 4 bits column by column while using approximate second-order (Hessian) information to update the not-yet-quantized weights and compensate for rounding error, using only a small calibration set.",
